            "label": {
              "000005QT": "Costs, SEK thousands",
              "000005QV": "Land area linked to costs, in hectare",
              "000005QU": "Of which productive forest land, in hectare"
            },
            "note": {
              "000005QT": [
                "The Swedish Environmental Protection Agencys costs for environmental protection consist partly of costs for administration of existing national parks and nature reserves and partly of costs for land redemption when the new protected areas are formed. These costs can be for purchases, compensation to the landowner for intrusion, subsidies for acquisition to municipalities and foundations or compensation for intrusion of land for the purpose of nature conservation. Costs are reported in thousands of SEK. The numbers are also rounded to even 100s."
              ],
              "000005QV": [
                "Because the information refers to both existing and future parks and reserves, it is not consistent with the information on area in the other tables about protected areas. Negative areas may exist when land that was purchased in previous years has been exchanged.  Up to 2014 only total areas are shown."
              ]
            },
